{:edb/db-before-t 1524 :edb/db-after-t 1525 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534837 50 #inst "2026-10-08T08:33:54.742Z" 13194139534837 true] [17592186175720 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186175720 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" 13194139534837 false] [17592186175851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313662 13194139534837 true] [17592186175851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313683 13194139534837 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313669 13194139534837 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313674 13194139534837 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313677 13194139534837 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313641 13194139534837 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313648 13194139534837 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313655 13194139534837 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313680 13194139534837 true] [17592186176357 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534837 true] [17592186176357 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^{2} - 2t$. What is the total displacement of the particle between $t = 1$ and $t = 4$?" 13194139534837 false] [17592186176357 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}-2t.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=4?$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186176357 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[2(4)^{3}-(4)^{2}]-[2(1)^{3}-(1)^{2}] \\\\  & =[128-16]-[2-1] \\\\  & =112-1 \\\\  & =111.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=4$ is $111.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186176420 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534837 true] [17592186176420 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/aad42b26d165789da802c0f507e3445976f3269b4c77e8b47201fb043b08f1f6.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=6.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=3?$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186176420 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3576/Source/Images/q-49319.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t = 0$ the particle is located at the position $x = 6$. What is the position of the particle at time $t = 3$?" 13194139534837 false] [17592186176420 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=3$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,3].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(3)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=6$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=3.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(3)=6+5=11\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=11.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186292199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313673 13194139534837 true] [17592186313641 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313642 13194139534837 true] [17592186313641 1089 "q-121011" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313641 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534837 true] [17592186313641 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/18904539463b95f9d681f61f0d8f875ad0cb03b35d4037e75c227d4523502193.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313641 1113 #uuid "b3f4668a-4edd-5293-8ac3-235d3b4b17f5" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313641 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(1)=2,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=1$ to $t=5.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(5)=2+6=8.\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x=8.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313643 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313644 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313645 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313646 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313647 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1041 "selection" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313645 13194139534837 true] [17592186313642 1110 #uuid "b3ec097a-89