3194139534837 true] [17592186313655 1089 "q-121021" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313655 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534837 true] [17592186313655 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/1df00f421b20b101d1500b4e2f47054f0c79dcfd2d82585fb8fb3735adb71af5.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=5.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=9?$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313655 1113 #uuid "55417913-20d1-5b59-b127-b0434ab8a445" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313655 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=9$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,9].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(9)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=5,$ and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=9.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{9}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(9)=5+2=7.\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=9$ is $x=7.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313657 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313658 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313659 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313660 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313661 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1041 "selection" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313660 13194139534837 true] [17592186313656 1110 #uuid "c1635112-b271-5528-8250-4bb9d0e77aa6" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313657 1034 "11" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313657 1111 #uuid "02746e22-a2df-59dd-99a0-842b242e0ff0" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313658 1034 "10" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313658 1111 #uuid "11a4c0b7-f40a-541c-9e80-512dd08b11b7" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313659 1034 "15" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313659 1111 #uuid "d48a861f-5c45-531a-866d-b1da683f296d" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313660 1034 "7" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313660 1111 #uuid "b74bb99c-6bd9-5a63-b500-5077523cd5da" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313661 1034 "2" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313661 1111 #uuid "91910ea5-90f3-59cb-9d33-de53185749df" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313662 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313663 13194139534837 true] [17592186313662 1089 "q-2413" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313662 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534837 true] [17592186313662 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=8{t}^{2}-3t.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=0$ and $t=6?$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313662 1113 #uuid "6b8f621e-5b34-573e-a1a6-210d53671902" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313662 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}(8{t}^{2}-3t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{8{t}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{8(6)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3(6)^{2}}{2}]-[\\frac{8(0)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3(0)^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =[576-54]-0 \\\\  & =522.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=6$ is $522.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313664 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313665 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313666 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313667 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313668 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1041 "selection" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313665 13194139534837 true] [17592186313663 1110 #uuid "69e392df-83c4-5a56-a1b3-33eba77f2001" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313664 1034 "505" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313664 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313664 1111 #uuid "d6da01a2-7096-5398-a354-f0a049a45ca9" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313665 1034 "522" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313665 1111 #uuid "46d0092a-58a8-5ae9-9579-1329976c9a1d" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313666 1034 "614" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313666 1111 #uuid "c0f6b683-fc28-507f-917f-1d2309511b8c" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313667 1034 "723" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313667 1111 #uuid "b4998c88-3576-54e3-96b0-bca5cfe0c6b3" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313668 1034 "494" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313668 1111 #uuid "dda457dc-16e9-506a-8ff3-44789d1dc710" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313669 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313670 13194139534837 true] [17592186313669 1089 "q-348283" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313669 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534837 true] [17592186313669 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ the particle is located at the position $x=1.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi .$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534837 true] [17592186313669 1113 #uuid "ee94a036-61d7-5666-86c5-e1e7634b5926" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313669 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =1+{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =1+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =1+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]) \\\\  & =1+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =1+(-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+1) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+1 \\\\  & =2+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=2+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313671 13194139534837 true] [17592186313670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313672 13194139534837 true] [17592186313670 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534837 true] [17592186313670 1041 "field-1" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313670 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313672 13194139534837 true] [17592186313670 1110 #uuid "a0c79e40-5b01-55dc-9e84-441be329e4a8" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313671 1034 "2" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313671 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313671 1111 #uuid "254a9d74-38b4-5ebe-8b77-8afcd3ad5b85" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313672 1034 "2+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313672 1111 #uuid "160d4a42-78a6-52b3-af93-d1e22f019900" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313673 1034 "4" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313673 1111 #uuid "91bfed64-4a4a-51e1-b6b5-5a4fcc6e7970" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313674 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313675 13194139534837 true] [17592186313674 1089 "q-351445" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313674 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534837 true] [17592186313674 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)={sec}^{2}⁡(t).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534837 true] [17592186313674 1113 #uuid "6032fcdd-918e-5031-92ae-a4aba1f32f4c" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313674 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-2+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2+{[\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =-2+1-0 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is $x=-1.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313675 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313676 13194139534837 true] [17592186313675 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534837 true] [17592186313675 1041 "field-1" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313675 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313676 13194139534837 true] [17592186313675 1110 #uuid "bdff4d62-4486-5bfb-b624-1b8a8ef0f6c8" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313676 1034 "-1" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313676 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313676 1111 #uuid "1adcae9f-211c-544a-9b62-3e2237f7ddbd" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313677 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313678 13194139534837 true] [17592186313677 1089 "q-351463" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313677 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534837 true] [17592186313677 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)={2}^{2t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=-5.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534837 true] [17592186313677 1113 #uuid "a0fdf1b5-7a2f-532e-9de1-59360bee3559" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313677 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=3$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,3].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(3)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(3) & =-5+{\\int }_{1}^{3}({2}^{2t-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-5+{[{2}^{2t-2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-5+{2}^{2(3)-2}-{2}^{2(1)-2} \\\\  & =-5+{2}^{4}-{2}^{0} \\\\  & =-5+16-1 \\\\  & =-5+15 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=3$ is $x=10.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313679 13194139534837 true] [17592186313678 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534837 true] [17592186313678 1041 "field-1" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313678 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313679 13194139534837 true] [17592186313678 1110 #uuid "6440dcae-32ae-5cfc-bcf2-af7fba314d3e" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313679 1034 "10" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313679 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313679 1111 #uuid "a52b41aa-89b5-5ed2-9c75-cbb2732e1af4" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313680 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313681 13194139534837 true] [17592186313680 1089 "q-351501" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313680 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534837 true] [17592186313680 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041851/assets/981252abc3668e62a5c9289c918d1231ec9a83745f70a00f0da4c85f194b8215.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=4,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534837 true] [17592186313680 1113 #uuid "8581a11a-e82d-5719-8003-6a34398d3c94" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313680 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=4$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [4,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(4)=-3$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=4$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=-3+3=0.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=0.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313681 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313682 13194139534837 true] [17592186313681 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534837 true] [17592186313681 1041 "field-1" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313681 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313682 13194139534837 true] [17592186313681 1110 #uuid "46040562-07d6-5906-8961-4bd2336ae6fa" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313682 1034 "0" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313682 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313682 1111 #uuid "23674bc9-cfa0-5690-8670-cdeda8a9fefb" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313683 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313684 13194139534837 true] [17592186313683 1089 "q-84263" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313683 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534837 true] [17592186313683 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=4\\sqrt[3]{t}-1.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=8?$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313683 1113 #uuid "2965e29b-870f-587a-8880-405fe07b35b2" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313683 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{8}(4\\sqrt[3]{t}-1)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3{t}^{4/3}-t){|}_{1}^{8} \\\\  & =[3(8)^{4/3}-8]-[3(1)^{4/3}-1] \\\\  & =[48-8]-[3-1] \\\\  & =40-2 \\\\  & =38.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=8$ is $38.$" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313685 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313686 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313687 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313688 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313689 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1041 "selection" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313686 13194139534837 true] [17592186313684 1110 #uuid "7170c817-ac0b-5c5b-b51c-db14fb759730" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313685 1034 "43" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313685 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313685 1111 #uuid "8fae7284-2cbf-5315-bf4c-4c9799f9f879" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313686 1034 "38" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313686 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313686 1111 #uuid "ddfc2c55-05ee-5a1b-998e-10e4eff4ab35" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313687 1034 "42" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534837 true] [17592186313687 1111 #uuid "c4cf4617-8b5a-5043-998c-e851c4574159" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313688 1034 "54" 13194139534837 true] [17592186313688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131941395